(4963749, 720110, 93565, '<td valign="top">Personally I like your entry more, although, as others have pointed out, I think a frontal view would be better. It also seems like things should be a little sharper, which is likely due to either the application of noise reduction or perhaps it just needed a little bit more sharpening, since a 1/2000 shutter should stop everything. Also, I wouldn''t think noise to be a huge issue at only 400, so maybe you were a bit heavy handed? Anyway, I did like your entry a good amount in the first place. Great timing and you did a great job following the prompt for the challenge.</td>', 'Personally I like your entry more, although, as others have pointed out, I think a frontal view would be better. It also seems like things should be a little sharper, which is likely due to either the application of noise reduction or perhaps it just needed a little bit more sharpening, since a 1/2000 shutter should stop everything. Also, I wouldn''t think noise to be a huge issue at only 400, so maybe you were a bit heavy handed? Anyway, I did like your entry a good amount in the first place. Great timing and you did a great job following the prompt for the challenge.', '2008-09-19 09:29:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(4963799, 719646, 82707, '<td valign="top">Thank-you ...............</td>', 'Thank-you ...............', '2008-09-19 09:55:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(4963812, 720110, 3936, '<td valign="top">As the others have already noted, the weak point of the image is that the dog is facing away from the camera.  Kinda like a crowd shot with only the backs of people''s heads.<br/> <br/>I like very much that you were able to keep the detail in the black fur of the dog.  Too many times they come out like black blobs.  <br/> <br/>The rest of the picture I would have liked a little bit brighter.  Not a whole lot brighter, just a bit. <br/> <br/>For the pixellation, try resizing in steps.  The newer software is better at it, but still has it''s limits.  By knocking it down and 10% or so, at a time, the software does not have to work as hard.  Not sure of all the mechanics of why, but it can help where you are having problems.</td>', 'As the others have already noted, the weak point of the image is that the dog is facing away from the camera.  Kinda like a crowd shot with only the backs of people''s heads. I like very much that you were able to keep the detail in the black fur of the dog.  Too many times they come out like black blobs.   The rest of the picture I would have liked a little bit brighter.  Not a whole lot brighter, just a bit.  For the pixellation, try resizing in steps.  The newer software is better at it, but still has it''s limits.  By knocking it down and 10% or so, at a time, the software does not have to work as hard.  Not sure of all the mechanics of why, but it can help where you are having problems.', '2008-09-19 09:58:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(4963863, 719646, 30982, '<td valign="top">The photographs is lovely, Judi, but the poem is truly priceless and heartbreaking.</td>', 'The photographs is lovely, Judi, but the poem is truly priceless and heartbreaking.', '2008-09-19 10:23:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(4964295, 719364, 66515, '<td valign="top">I have to ask: With a 50 mm macro, How friggin close were you??? :)</td>', 'I have to ask: With a 50 mm macro, How friggin close were you??? :)', '2008-09-19 14:10:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(4964300, 719364, 82112, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Citadel:</b></div><hr/><i> I have to ask: With a 50 mm macro, How friggin close were you??? :) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Couple of feet I''d say. This was a pretty tight crop of what I started with. But for some of the other photos I took, I was right in there with them, and it was a little disconcerting having them buzzing all about me.<br/> <br/>Ah, the stupid things we do for DPC!</td>', 'Originally posted by Citadel: I have to ask: With a 50 mm macro, How friggin close were you??? :)   Couple of feet I''d say. This was a pretty tight crop of what I started with. But for some of the other photos I took, I was right in there with them, and it was a little disconcerting having them buzzing all about me. Ah, the stupid things we do for DPC!', '2008-09-19 14:16:05.000000', NULL, 0),
