(4968850, 720132, 30982, '<td valign="top">LOL about the thing flying around!  Congrats on a lovely shot, a new personal best, and a 5th in a very big challenge!</td>', 'LOL about the thing flying around!  Congrats on a lovely shot, a new personal best, and a 5th in a very big challenge!', '2008-09-22 17:27:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(4968853, 718378, 30982, '<td valign="top">There''s a fly AND an ant!  Lovely work and congrats on a top ten!</td>', 'There''s a fly AND an ant!  Lovely work and congrats on a top ten!', '2008-09-22 17:30:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(4968910, 718164, 86090, '<td valign="top">**Greetings from the critic club***<br/> <br/>I think you did a good job in use a narrow DOF, isolating you subject and making it stand out. By looking at you setting I can see that you were shooting in low light, wich has caused some noise on your background, I would also have prefered a smother transition between the two colors. Sometimes it''s better to wait for a better light condition, so you can use a lower ISO and a faster shutter wich will allow you to get a sharper image.<br/> <br/>Now about the composition, I think is pleasing, but it might work better if you fill the frame a bit more with your subject and moving it a little bit more to one of the sides, instead of entering the frame exactly by the corner.<br/> <br/>I hope this helps.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-09-22 20:55:02.</i></td>', '**Greetings from the critic club*** I think you did a good job in use a narrow DOF, isolating you subject and making it stand out. By looking at you setting I can see that you were shooting in low light, wich has caused some noise on your background, I would also have prefered a smother transition between the two colors. Sometimes it''s better to wait for a better light condition, so you can use a lower ISO and a faster shutter wich will allow you to get a sharper image. Now about the composition, I think is pleasing, but it might work better if you fill the frame a bit more with your subject and moving it a little bit more to one of the sides, instead of entering the frame exactly by the corner. I hope this helps.', '2008-09-22 18:29:17.000000', '2008-09-22 21:55:02.000000', 0),
(4969252, 720289, 60862, '<td valign="top">What a fun shot!  And I love the title. :)</td>', 'What a fun shot!  And I love the title. :)', '2008-09-22 23:02:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(4969494, 719659, 86090, '<td valign="top">***Greetings from the critic club***<br/> <br/>Congrats on your first entry, you got a nice score.<br/> <br/>I thinks you did a good use of DOF, wich helps to isolate your subject, though I migh have worked better if you have filled the frame a bit more with your subject to show more detail, also, the focus seems a bit off, this might have something to do with your shutter speed, since theses little guys tend to move fast, you need a faster shutter speed.<br/> <br/>About the editing, you might want to try lowering a bit the saturations on the greens.<br/> <br/>I hope this helps.<br/> <br/></td>', '***Greetings from the critic club*** Congrats on your first entry, you got a nice score. I thinks you did a good use of DOF, wich helps to isolate your subject, though I migh have worked better if you have filled the frame a bit more with your subject to show more detail, also, the focus seems a bit off, this might have something to do with your shutter speed, since theses little guys tend to move fast, you need a faster shutter speed. About the editing, you might want to try lowering a bit the saturations on the greens. I hope this helps. ', '2008-09-23 02:48:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(4969731, 719859, 50641, '<td valign="top">Coolest caterpillar shot I''ve ever seen.  It''s so hard to get their ''face'' in focus - but you nailed it!  Colors are splendiforous.  Congrats on the high score and top ten!</td>', 'Coolest caterpillar shot I''ve ever seen.  It''s so hard to get their ''face'' in focus - but you nailed it!  Colors are splendiforous.  Congrats on the high score and top ten!', '2008-09-23 11:17:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(4969831, 720000, 68573, '<td valign="top">Very creative, well conceptualised, and ''crazily:)''executed. Well done Irene</td>', 'Very creative, well conceptualised, and ''crazily:)''executed. Well done Irene', '2008-09-23 12:33:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(4970303, 720072, 15291, '<td valign="top">Hi Konrad,<br/>         First let me say you have a nice image here. You did a really nice job with the dof &amp; it fits the challange to a tee. I like the composition, your model is posed well and the little bit of tree showing is a nice touch. The focus looks to be tac sharp &amp; has nice detail. The lighting seems to be just a bit off balance mainly in the chest area and left shoulder &amp; arm washing out some of the skin tones. The lighting in the facial area seems better &amp; has more skin tone. I like the catch light &amp; the bit of glare on her lip is a plus. Over all this is a really nice image, with a few minor lighting adjustments this would be fantastic.</td>', 'Hi Konrad,         First let me say you have a nice image here. You did a really nice job with the dof & it fits the challange to a tee. I like the composition, your model is posed well and the little bit of tree showing is a nice touch. The focus looks to be tac sharp & has nice detail. The lighting seems to be just a bit off balance mainly in the chest area and left shoulder & arm washing out some of the skin tones. The lighting in the facial area seems better & has more skin tone. I like the catch light & the bit of glare on her lip is a plus. Over all this is a really nice image, with a few minor lighting adjustments this would be fantastic.', '2008-09-23 16:42:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(4970364, 720166, 15291, '<td valign="top">Hi Bob,<br/>      First let me say you have a nice image here. I really like your use of dof here it is excellent both front &amp; back. I like the way the image is composed, the offset &amp; sideway shutters really make the image work. I like the color balance they all work well together.<br/>The focus seems nice and sharp with plenty of detail &amp; texture. The only distraction I see  and it is minor is the first white shutter though out of focus it kept catching my eye. Overall this is a really nice image it is simple yet effective, and it has interest.</td>', 'Hi Bob,      First let me say you have a nice image here. I really like your use of dof here it is excellent both front & back. I like the way the image is composed, the offset & sideway shutters really make the image work. I like the color balance they all work well together.The focus seems nice and sharp with plenty of detail & texture. The only distraction I see  and it is minor is the first white shutter though out of focus it kept catching my eye. Overall this is a really nice image it is simple yet effective, and it has interest.', '2008-09-23 17:09:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(4970858, 720079, 67697, '<td valign="top">Oooh this is gorgeous.  I didn''t vote so I did not see this.  Love the blend of fall colors too.</td>', 'Oooh this is gorgeous.  I didn''t vote so I did not see this.  Love the blend of fall colors too.', '2008-09-23 22:56:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(4971041, 720289, 97270, '<td valign="top">For the <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/challenge_results.php?CHALLENGE_ID=916&amp;show_full=1" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Shallow DOF IV</a> challenge,<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=96534" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//lh3.ggpht.com/prash.chopra/SMnHDBO1dvI/AAAAAAAAENo/fbeE6nRFY6g/s400/DPC-PrashTrophy.jpg'', strrpos(''//lh3.ggpht.com/prash.chopra/SMnHDBO1dvI/AAAAAAAAENo/fbeE6nRFY6g/s400/DPC-PrashTrophy.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//lh3.ggpht.com/prash.chopra/SMnHDBO1dvI/AAAAAAAAENo/fbeE6nRFY6g/s400/DPC-PrashTrophy.jpg"/></a> to <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=720289" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/916/120/720289.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/916/120/720289.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/916/120/720289.jpg"/></a> by <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=96534" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">jettyimages</a> <br/> <br/>Note: This rank was given after the voting period was over.<br/></td>', 'For the Shallow DOF IV challenge,  to  by  jettyimages  Note: This rank was given after the voting period was over.', '2008-09-24 00:40:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(4971688, 719529, 30982, '<td valign="top">If you hadn''t mentioned the glass, I''d never have known - you did a very good job disguising that fact!  And this guy is adorable!  Very good use of shallow depth of field!</td>', 'If you hadn''t mentioned the glass, I''d never have known - you did a very good job disguising that fact!  And this guy is adorable!  Very good use of shallow depth of field!', '2008-09-24 08:55:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(4973472, 720059, 79955, '<td valign="top">Was supposed to leave you a comment after the challenge, almost forgot.<br/>The image has a nice persepective which is always a good start. Composition is also good.<br/>The improvement areas (potential)<br/>- The highlights are overblown , would recomment a different background (prob a darker one)<br/>   A darker one will also help contrast against the gutar strings.<br/>- Your point of focus is just not crip enough<br/>- also the subject that you choose to photograph also needs to have more contrasting colors.<br/> <br/>One other thing , IMO , the shot needs to be a little more symmetrical. This is my opinon only.. Andrew</td>', 'Was supposed to leave you a comment after the challenge, almost forgot.The image has a nice persepective which is always a good start. Composition is also good.The improvement areas (potential)- The highlights are overblown , would recomment a different background (prob a darker one)   A darker one will also help contrast against the gutar strings.- Your point of focus is just not crip enough- also the subject that you choose to photograph also needs to have more contrasting colors. One other thing , IMO , the shot needs to be a little more symmetrical. This is my opinon only.. Andrew', '2008-09-24 20:48:33.000000', NULL, 0),
